# GENIE.AI SLIM lock for the retriever microservice (issue #2000).
#
# Same source tree, same behaviour — the SLIM variant only changes WHAT THE
# FINAL IMAGE INSTALLS. The fat lock (requirements-cpu.txt) resolves
# `torch==2.13.0` to the CUDA/cu13 build (15 `nvidia-*` wheels + triton,
# ~3.8 GB compressed in the pip layer), because `uv pip compile` resolves the
# Linux torch wheel from PyPI, where it IS the CUDA build.
#
# The retriever DOES have a local-model path — `HuggingFaceBgeEmbeddings`
# (genieai_retriever_arangodb.py, the `else` branch of the embedding
# selection) loads a sentence-transformers model in-process when no remote
# embedding endpoint is configured. So torch stays — but CPU-only: the
# `+cpu` local build, from the PyTorch CPU index, at the SAME version
# (2.13.0). The local-model path keeps working; only the device changes
# (CPU instead of CUDA), which is what a deployment without a GPU needs.
#
# EVERY version below is the version the FAT lock pins — the slim image must
# not drift from the fat one on anything but torch. (A fresh resolve pulled
# numpy 2.4.6 / openai 2.54 against the fat lock's numpy 1.26.4 / openai
# 1.109.1: same source, different runtime. The pins below remove that
# freedom on purpose; the TRANSITIVE dependencies still float, and are
# hash-pinned in the compiled lock.)
#
# DELTAS vs requirements-cpu.txt:
#   - torch: CUDA/cu13 build -> CPU build (+cpu). Drops the 15 `nvidia-*`
#     wheels and triton (~3 GB compressed).
#   - dropped: docling, docling-core, docling-ibm-models, easyocr,
#     graspologic, einops, bs4, docx2txt, cairosvg, decord, pathway,
#     neo4j, mariadb, pgvector, opensearch-py, pymilvus, qdrant-haystack,
#     redis, the whole `llama-index-*` tree, and the `langchain-{community,
#     milvus, elasticsearch, mariadb, opengauss, pinecone}` family — none of
#     them is imported by the retriever's runtime chain (ArangoVector,
#     HuggingFaceBgeEmbeddings, HuggingFaceEndpointEmbeddings, ChatOpenAI,
#     OpenAIEmbeddings, ArangoClient, the comps core).
#   - docarray[full] -> docarray (the "full" extra pulls trimesh, av, jax,
#     pandas, pydub, lz4, protobuf; the vendored
#     `comps/cores/proto/docarray.py` only needs the BASE package).
#
# Regenerate with (the CPU index FIRST, and `unsafe-best-match` because uv's
# default `first-index` stops at PyPI, where torch==2.13.0 IS the CUDA
# build, and never reaches the CPU index's 2.13.0+cpu):
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.11 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_31 \
#     --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu \
#     --extra-index-url https://pypi.org/simple \
#     --index-strategy unsafe-best-match \
#     requirements-slim.in -o requirements-slim.txt

